From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: ROG5 apply video-mode perf votes before the encoders start

drm_atomic_helper_commit_modeset_enables() enables the CRTC, then the
encoders; a video-mode encoder starts the INTF timing engine in its enable,
but dpu_core_perf_crtc_update() only runs in atomic_flush afterwards. The
first frames therefore scan out on the previous (low) bus/clock votes. On
the ROG5 DP output (USB-C HDMI hub, 1080p60, DSI panel off) INTF_0 underran
from the first frame and kept underrunning on every frame (380/380) even
after the votes were raised (bus 4 GB/s via 0100), until the next modeset,
after which 0/314. With the votes fixed before the enable (debugfs fixed
perf mode) there was no underrun either.

Apply the new performance state in dpu_crtc_enable() for CRTCs driving a
video-mode encoder, before the encoders are enabled.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c	2026-09-29 15:38:28.260808836 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c	2026-09-29 15:38:28.274383127 +0200
@@ -1309,6 +1309,17 @@
 	trace_dpu_crtc_enable(DRMID(crtc), true, dpu_crtc);
 	dpu_crtc->enabled = true;
 
+	/*
+	 * The encoders are enabled after the CRTC, and a video-mode encoder
+	 * starts its timing engine there, before atomic_flush applies the
+	 * votes computed in atomic_check. Scanning out on the old (low) bus
+	 * and clock votes, INTF_0 (DP on the ROG5) underran from the first
+	 * frame and stayed in underrun until the next modeset. Apply the new
+	 * performance state before the encoders start.
+	 */
+	if (request_bandwidth)
+		dpu_core_perf_crtc_update(crtc, 1);
+
 	if (!old_crtc_state->self_refresh_active) {
 		drm_for_each_encoder_mask(encoder, crtc->dev, crtc->state->encoder_mask)
 			dpu_encoder_assign_crtc(encoder, crtc);
